                <pb facs="0247" n="191" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg191"/>

                <head>(M. 4201.)<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. W.
                            Inman to Board of Trade</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Inman Steamship Company</hi>, (<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >limited</hi>,) <hi rendition="#small-caps">late Liverpool, New York
                                and Philadelphia Steamship Company</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Liverpool</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-03-16"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 16,
                        1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your letter of the 19th
                    February, (M. 2626,) I have now the honor to inclose, in compliance therewith,
                    the following reports, namely: From Mr. James Kennedy, master of the steamship
                    City of Berlin; from Mr. Samuel Brooks, master of the steamship City of
                    Richmond; from Mr. Robert Leitch, master of the steamship City of Chester; from
                    Mr. John Mirehouse, master of the steamship City of Montreal; from Mr. Henry
                    Tibbits, master of the steamship City of Paris; and from Mr. George S. Murray,
                    master of the steamship City of Brooklyn; and I have only further to remark that
                    these are all masters of great experience, who have been in this company’s
                    service for twenty years, and on whose opinions I place every reliance.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WILLIAM INMAN.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Assistant Secretary</hi><lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Marine Department, Board of Trade</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>








